{"content":"Fixed — the magic `+ 700` char window is gone. The upper bound is now anchored on structural markers instead of an arbitrary distance:

```dart
final nextBulletAt = finalizeGateContractPrompt.indexOf(
  '\n- **',
  bulletAt + 1,
);
final paragraphEndAt = finalizeGateContractPrompt.indexOf(
  '\n\n',
  bulletAt + 1,
);
final upperBound = [
  if (nextBulletAt != -1) nextBulletAt,
  if (paragraphEndAt != -1) paragraphEndAt,
].fold(
  finalizeGateContractPrompt.length,
  (a, b) => a < b ? a : b,
);
expect(refAt, lessThan(upperBound));
```

One adaptation to the suggested snippet: the "Content, not existence" bullet is the **last** bullet in the named-checks section, so a bare `indexOf('\n- **', …)` returns `-1`; the paragraph end (`\n\n`) covers that case. Net effect is exactly the intended guard: a legitimate bullet extension or generator re-wrap can no longer fail the test, while a move into the next bullet — or past the section — now fails. Location: `test/cli/finalize_gate_prompt_test.dart`, `gh-1668 C3`.
